sentences.t:
Inde alios ineunt cursus aliosque recursus
adversi spatiis, alternosque orbibus orbes
impediunt, pugnaeque cient simulacra sub armis;

sentences.l:
Then other courses they enter and other courses back,
facing one another in their spaces, and alternating with circles, circles
they entangle, and of battle they stir up images under arms;

sentences.t:
Ast illae diversa metu per litora passim
diffugiunt, silvasque et sicubi concava furtim
saxa petunt;

sentences.l:
But they, in fear, over the scattered shores, here and there
flee apart, and the woods, and wherever hollow, secretly,
rocks, they seek;
